Inject a narrow fetcher (object seam) with a production default:<br/><pre>interface UserSource { listActive(): Promise&lt;User[]&gt; }
const dbUsers: UserSource = {
  listActive: () =&gt; db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE active = true'),
};
async function activeUserCount(src: UserSource = dbUsers): Promise&lt;number&gt; {
  const rows = await src.listActive();
  return rows.length;
}</pre>Production still calls <code>activeUserCount()</code> (uses <code>dbUsers</code>). Test:<br/><pre>test('counts active rows', async () =&gt; {
  const fake: UserSource = { listActive: async () =&gt; [u1, u2, u3] };
  expect(await activeUserCount(fake)).toBe(3);
});</pre>The enabling point is the parameter; only the one dependency the test needs was extracted, and no global persistence layer was designed.

